From 174da2b81debe7fc80c4ad97cecb95f18903e9dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:20:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): rate a hole op by the lower of the material
 row and the running feed

A Drill or Thread op is now rated by the lower of two values when the
material in force on its setup is the document's material: the tool's
cutting-data row for that material, and the tool's running feed. Before,
a running feed lowered below a row that names the material did not reach
the rating, so an op at the row feed posted with no refusal.

The seed of a new or retargeted Drill or Thread op uses the same rating,
so a seeded op is never refused by the post check. A stock that states
its own material keeps the rating of its own row.

Pinned by hole_feed_rating::a_running_feed_lowered_below_the_material_row_is_the_rating.

Fixes #2724

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
